## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "8mA"
  total_current_limit: "300mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "ALL GPIO pins on TM4C1294NCPDT are 3.3V ONLY — none are 5V tolerant; applying 5V logic to any pin causes latch-up or permanent damage; always use a level-shifting buffer (e.g. TXB0108) between Teensy/5V Arduino and TM4C1294"
    - "PD7 and PF0 are NMI-LOCKED by default — write GPIOLOCK=0x4C4F434B then GPIOCR=0xFF to the respective port before using PD7 or PF0 as GPIO; PF0 is also the on-board LED D4 and requires unlock for GPIO use"
    - "PC0-PC3 (TCK, TMS, TDI, TDO/SWO) are dedicated JTAG/SWD pins — do NOT reassign unless JTAG is fully and intentionally disabled; disabling JTAG permanently prevents use of the on-board ICDI debugger until re-flashed via UART bootloader"
    - "Both CAN buses (CAN0: PA0/PA1 or PB4/PB5; CAN1: PB0/PB1) require an external transceiver chip (TI SN65HVD232 or ISO1042) — the MCU outputs 3.3V CMOS levels; the EK-TM4C1294XL board has NO on-board CAN transceiver"
    - "UART0 (PA0/PA1) is shared with the on-board ICDI virtual COM port — when ICDI USB is connected, PA0/PA1 receive drive from the ICDI UART bridge; do NOT connect external UART devices to PA0/PA1 while using the ICDI serial console"
    - "I2C9 shares pins PA0/PA1 with UART0 and CAN0 — enabling I2C9 on PA0/PA1 simultaneously with UART0 or CAN0 on the same pins will cause bus contention and data corruption; select the desired function exclusively via GPIO peripheral mux"
    - "The on-chip Ethernet PHY has dedicated power supply requirements — the PHY runs from an internal 1.2V LDO; external decoupling capacitors on the PHY supply pins are mandatory per TI layout guidelines; poor decoupling causes link instability at 100Mbps"
    - "The EPI (External Peripheral Interface) can drive SDRAM, SRAM or HOST-BUS but its pins (PK0-PK7, PH0-PH3 etc.) overlap with ADC inputs, I2C and UART — enabling EPI disables all overlapping peripheral functions; plan resource allocation before layout"
    - "The on-board Ethernet RJ45 connector uses integrated magnetics — do NOT substitute a bare-pin RJ45 connector without adding discrete magnetics; the Ethernet PHY requires 1:1 isolation transformers per IEEE 802.3 for proper operation and EMC compliance"
compatibility:
  sw: "Code Composer Studio (CCS) v6+; IAR Embedded Workbench; Keil MDK-ARM; Energia (Arduino-compatible); PlatformIO (tivac target)"
  languages: "C;C++;ARM assembly;Energia (C++ subset)"
  frameworks: "TivaWare for C Series 2.1+;LwIP;FreeRTOS;TI-RTOS;CMSIS;Energia"
  certifications: "FCC;CE;RoHS"

